# Only gitignored, machine-local material is excluded. Every TRACKED file must
# stay in the context: buildinfo's build script runs `git status --porcelain`
# to decide the `-dirty` version suffix, and a tracked file missing from the
# context would look deleted and stamp every image as dirty. (And at least one
# tracked non-source file is compiled in: crates/blorb include_bytes!'s
# unit_tests/macfont.hfs.) `.git` itself is kept, deliberately, so the binary
# carries its own short hash.
target/
stories/
masterpieces
treasures
node_modules/
.worktrees/
.claude/
.superpowers/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
docker-compose.override.yml
